# ObservableToTaskBridgeSites.allow — the SEEDED inventory of `.ToTask(` call sites, for
# ObservableToTaskBridgeGuard. One `relative/path.cs<TAB>count` per line; `#` starts a comment.
#
# 🚨 THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Adding a line is not a fix — the guard fails on a new file, a
# raised count, or a raised TOTAL, and TotalBudget in the guard must be lowered by the same
# amount whenever an entry is deleted or lowered.
#
# It covers ONLY the trees whose sweep is still in flight: `test/` and `memex/`.
# `src/`, `tools/`, `samples/` and `clients/` are held at ZERO with NO allow file at all
# (maintainer, 2026-08-30: "no ToTask ever"; "in src especially we should have zero"), so there
# is deliberately no line here you could add for them. When a wave empties one of the two roots
# above, move it into the guard's ProductionRoots and delete its lines here.
#
# Counts are produced by the guard's own scanner, with comments and string literals masked — so a
# doc comment quoting the banned shape (this repo does that at length, on purpose, to explain WHY
# it is banned) is not a site and must never be edited to satisfy a textual scan.
